{"sounds":{"intro":"Romani is the language of the Roma people, who live across Europe and beyond. It comes from India (it is a cousin of Hindi and Punjabi) and has many dialects: Vlax, Balkan, Sinti, Carpathian and more. This pack uses a Vlax-style (Kalderash) spelling with a Latin respelling in the \"say\" line. Dialects differ a lot in vocabulary and sound.","rows":[["č","\"ch\" as in \"church\"","čhavo"],["š","\"sh\" as in \"shop\"","šukar"],["ž","\"s\" as in \"measure\"","žanav"],["x","\"kh\" like \"ch\" in Scottish \"loch\"","xav"],["ʰ","a puff of breath after the letter","čhon"]],"notes":["Many Roma are bilingual, and the spelling here is one of several in use. There is no single standard Romani. Expect real speakers to say words differently.","This pool is much smaller than the Spanish one on purpose and has not been checked by a Romani speaker."]},"numbers":[{"id":"1-to-10","title":"1 to 10","items":[["one","jekh","yekh"],["two","duj","dooy"],["three","trin","treen"],["four","štar","shtar"],["five","panč","panch"],["six","šov","shov"],["seven","efta","EF-ta"],["eight","oxto","OKH-to"],["nine","enja","EN-ya"],["ten","deš","desh"]]}],"greetings":[{"id":"greetings-and-politeness","title":"Greetings and politeness","items":[["hello / good day","Lačho dive","LA-cho DEE-veh"],["good morning","Lačhi sabah","LA-chee sa-BAH"],["good evening","Lačhi rjat","LA-chee RYAT"],["welcome","Aven baxtale","A-ven bakh-TA-leh"],["how are you?","Sar san?","sar san"],["I'm fine","Mištó som","mish-TO som"],["goodbye","Te aves baxtalo","teh A-ves bakh-TA-lo"],["thank you","Del o Del tuke","del o del TOO-keh"],["please","Mangav tut","MAN-gav toot"],["yes","Va","va"],["no","Na","na"]]}],"phrases":[{"id":"about-me","title":"About me","items":[["I","me","meh"],["you","tu","too"],["he / she","vo / voj","vo / voy"],["we","amen","A-men"],["they","von","von"],["I am a student","Me som studento","meh som stoo-DEN-to"],["I am a teacher","Me som sikavno","meh som SEE-kav-no"],["my name is Eric","Mi anav si Eric","mee A-nav see Eric"],["what's your name?","Sar akhardjol?","sar a-KHAR-jol"],["I know","Me žanav","meh ZHA-nav"],["I don't know","Me na žanav","meh na ZHA-nav"],["I want","Me kamav","meh KA-mav"],["I don't want","Me na kamav","meh na KA-mav"],["I eat","Me xav","meh khav"],["I don't eat","Me na xav","meh na khav"]]}],"vocab":[{"id":"people-and-family","title":"People and family","items":[["father","dad","dad"],["mother","daj","day"],["son / boy","čhavo","CHA-vo"],["daughter / girl","čhaj","chay"],["brother","phral","phral"],["sister","pheň","phen"],["man / husband","rom","rom"],["woman / wife","romni","ROM-nee"],["person","manuš","MA-noosh"]]},{"id":"nature-and-things","title":"Nature and things","items":[["sun","kham","kham"],["moon","čhon","chon"],["water","pani","PA-nee"],["fire","jag","yag"],["earth","phuv","phoov"],["bread","maro","MA-ro"],["meat","mas","mas"],["milk","thud","thood"],["house","kher","kher"],["village","gav","gav"],["road","drom","drom"],["horse","grast","grast"],["hand","vast","vast"],["eye","jakh","yakh"],["language / tongue","čhib","chib"],["word","lav","lav"]]},{"id":"describing","title":"Describing","items":[["good","lačho","LA-cho"],["beautiful","šukar","shoo-KAR"],["big","baro","BA-ro"],["small","tikno","TEEK-no"],["new","nevo","NEH-vo"],["old","phuro","PHOO-ro"],["black","kalo","KA-lo"],["white","parno","PAR-no"],["red","lolo","LO-lo"]]},{"id":"verbs-stem","title":"Verbs (stem)","items":[["to do","ker-","ker"],["to eat","xa-","kha"],["to drink","pi-","pee"],["to go","dža-","ja"],["to come","av-","av"],["to see","dikh-","dikh"],["to say","phen-","phen"],["to know","džan-","jan"],["to sleep","sov-","sov"]]}],"grammar":[{"id":"pronouns","title":"Pronouns","text":["Romani verbs change by person: -av (I), -es (you), -el (he/she), -as (we), -en (you pl. and they) in the present for most verbs."],"rows":[["I","me","meh"],["you","tu","too"],["he","vo","vo"],["she","voj","voy"],["we","amen","A-men"],["they","von","von"]],"ex":[["I am a rom","Me som rom","meh som rom"],["you are a student","Tu san studento","too san stoo-DEN-to"],["he is a teacher","Vo si sikavno","vo see SEE-kav-no"]]},{"id":"present-tense-xa-to-eat","title":"Present tense (xa- to eat)","text":["Take the stem and add the person ending."],"rows":[["I eat","xav","khav"],["you eat","xas","khas"],["he eats","xal","khal"],["we eat","xas","khas"],["they eat","xan","khan"]],"ex":[["I eat bread","Me xav maro","meh khav MA-ro"],["he eats meat","Vo xal mas","vo khal mas"],["we eat","Amen xas","A-men khas"]]},{"id":"negation","title":"Negation","text":["Put \"na\" before the verb: \"me na xav\" (I do not eat). \"Nane\" means \"there is not\". For a command, use \"ma\": \"ma xa\" (do not eat)."],"rows":[["not","na","na"],["there is not","nane","NA-neh"],["do not (command)","ma","ma"]],"ex":[["I eat","Me xav","meh khav"],["I do not eat","Me na xav","meh na khav"],["eat!","Xa!","kha"],["do not eat!","Ma xa!","ma kha"]]}],"name":"Romani","id":"rom","flag":"rom","note":""}